  <body>
    <header><a href="/">← TOTO GLOBAL DESK</a><h1>Editorial Standards</h1></header>
    <main>
      <h2>Prime directive</h2>
      <p>Investigate aggressively. Publish with discipline. <strong>Credibility is the only asset that compounds.</strong></p>

      <h2>How we label claims</h2>
      <p>Every material claim in our reporting carries one of these classifications:</p>
      <p>
        <span class="label" style="color:#166534">Confirmed fact</span>
        <span class="label" style="color:#1d4ed8">Primary document</span>
        <span class="label" style="color:#1e40af">Official statement</span>
        <span class="label" style="color:#4c1d95">Court ruling</span>
        <span class="label" style="color:#b45309">Charge</span>
        <span class="label" style="color:#dc2626">Allegation</span>
        <span class="label" style="color:#92400e">Ongoing investigation</span>
        <span class="label" style="color:#6b7280">Media report</span>
        <span class="label" style="color:#7c3aed">Analysis</span>
        <span class="label" style="color:#991b1b">Unverified claim</span>
      </p>

      <h2>Hard rules</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Never convert an allegation into a finding through headline, placement, or repetition.</li>
        <li>No implication of guilt without evidence meeting the classification standard.</li>
        <li>Headlines may not be stronger than the story's evidence.</li>
        <li>Contested matters show: <strong>what is known, what is claimed, what documents show, what remains unconfirmed, and what different sides say.</strong></li>
        <li>No partisan framing in news copy; analysis lives in clearly labeled sections.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Sourcing</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Primary first:</strong> we attempt to locate the underlying document before publishing any material claim.</li>
        <li><strong>Two-source rule:</strong> significant claims require two independent sources, or one primary document plus one report.</li>
        <li><strong>Anti-circular:</strong> ten outlets repeating one report is one source. We trace to origin.</li>
        <li>Social media is treated as a lead — never as evidence.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>Errors are corrected visibly: what was wrong, what changed, when, why, and the supporting source. We never silently rewrite published errors. Corrections appear on the article and in a public log.</p>

      <h2>What-changed discipline</h2>
      <p>Every update to a developing story opens with <strong>what changed</strong> since our previous report. No material change means no alert — even when a story is "in the news."</p>

      <h2>Breaking news</h2>
      <p>We publish BREAKING only for material events: major rulings, major official decisions, major enforcement actions, confirmed investigation developments, policy changes, military/security events, resignations or deaths of major figures, significant emergencies. Never because a keyword trended.</p>

      <h2>Independence</h2>
      <p>This is a personal newsroom with a published watchlist. Coverage includes uncomfortable facts for every side. The desk serves the reader's curiosity — not a party line.</p>
    </main>
    <footer>TOTO GLOBAL DESK · International News • Intelligence • Investigations</footer>
